  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 122 PM MST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nUpper level ridge axis moves to the Wyoming border overnight and\nsouthwesterly flow aloft begins with extensive high and mid\nlevel clouds overnight into Wednesday ahead of a system moving\nwell to the north. Dry conditions continue through Wednesday\nnight and flow turns more zonal allowing more moisture into the\nregion in earnest Thursday through Friday. Expecting\nprecipitation mainly in the central mountains and eastern\nmountains in this period with very snow levels around 7 thousand\nfeet maybe dropping to around 5000 to 5500 late Friday. Not\nexpecting heavy snow with under 3 inches below 7 thousand feet\nthrough Friday night. Snake River Plain will see very light rain\nthrough the period as well. Much lighter precipitation is now\nexpected late weekend as models backing off on precipitation\namounts significantly. So will see a bit more impactful weather\nbeginning Thanksgiving day but not expecting any significant\nimpacts through this weekend. Significant winds are not expected\nthrough the next 7 days.",
